2026-09-27T07:46:17.0619830Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0620366Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0620810Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0622016Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0623342Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0623521Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0623845Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0624282Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0624676Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0624837Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0625171Z ================
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0625346Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0625630Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0626209Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0626530Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0626743Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0627191Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0627633Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0627875Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0628467Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0628995Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0630001Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0630937Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0631153Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0631808Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0632724Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0633195Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0633739Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0634416Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0634592Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0634929Z ========
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0635100Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0637277Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0639770Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0640141Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0640944Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0642203Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0643288Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0644285Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0645120Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0645825Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0646031Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0646474Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0646717Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0649014Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0733940Z 
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0735100Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0736479Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:46:17.0736806Z 
